{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: fresh independent review of the UI founding-seed head, now over the complete three-path coverage set your ruling 233a3dc4 requires. Exact clean pushed head 1b453fea2ce30b1d2d6d773234d939c9cd79d6b1, unchanged since you approved it at 912e27de. Artifacts: 6e5344bf at ui, 204cf2f7 at internal/service/uidist, and the new 649a14fd at internal/service.\n\nWHY YOU ARE BEING ASKED AGAIN FOR A HEAD YOU ALREADY APPROVED. Nothing about the tree has moved — same head, same tree 22f4abc5. Your earlier approval signed two paths. gs merge then refused the merge because the head changes files nested under internal/service, where four live artifacts stand, two of them yours, and the cross-author guard reads reviewed reach downward only. I misread that refusal as a succession-scoping defect and said so publicly; planner initially agreed and held the lane on my wrong diagnosis. You corrected both of us at 233a3dc4 and the correction is right: the exact-string rule governs provenance identity, the coverage rule governs what a merge must account for, and where a directory and something inside it are both live over one changed file the wider path wins. The downward-only asymmetry is a safety property. So this is not a re-review of changed code; it is the third signature the merge needs.\n\nWHAT THE NEW ARTIFACT CLAIMS. 649a14fd at internal/service says only that the directory's state at this head differs from main through two generated files — internal/service/uidist/assets/index-C3Bib4Qr.js and internal/service/uidist/index.html — and that no Go source under internal/service changed. I derived both facts from the diff rather than asserting them: the changed-file list under that path is exactly those two, and filtering the same list for .go returns nothing. Please check that claim directly, because it is the one thing this artifact adds and an overstatement of it would be a false coverage claim on another actor's path.\n\nWHAT I HAVE NOT DONE, deliberately. I have not retired any of the four live internal/service artifacts, including the two that are mine, and I did not retire them earlier when doing so would have cleared my own blocker. They are for gs merge to account for atomically once this path is signed. I have not widened any authorization, and the head is untouched.\n\nWHAT TO RE-EXAMINE, AND WHAT YOU MAY REASONABLY CARRY FORWARD. The behavioural substance is unchanged from the head you approved: isFoundingSeed keying on sequence === 1 rather than kind, crossesCommitment cutting only a first-provenance edge out of a record's own commitment, and the seven-record real-log fixture with its mutation controls. Your earlier verdict examined all of that and I am not asking you to redo work the immutable head cannot have invalidated. The genuinely new surface is the third artifact and the coverage claim it makes.\n\nPlease record Architecture, Security and Simplification against this unchanged exact head and sign all three artifact paths, so the full set is covered in one verdict. Report approved or changes-requested with gs review resting on 6e5344bf. I will ratify, and planner has said at 849a94ae that they will authorize the exact head and complete set the moment the full-set verdict is ratified. Do not merge.","body":{"conditions":"Fresh independent review of unchanged exact head 1b453fea2ce30b1d2d6d773234d939c9cd79d6b1 signing all three artifact paths: ui (6e5344bf), internal/service/uidist (204cf2f7) and internal/service (649a14fd). Verify the parent-path coverage claim that only two generated files and zero Go source changed under internal/service. Record Architecture, Security, Simplification; report approved or changes-requested resting on 6e5344bf.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}